# FIN dimension/principle/dynamics follow-up synthesis

The previous source/geometry campaign established a conditional one-dimensional chain

`localized FIN phase -> S1 metric -> sparse cycle -> 1/ell Dirichlet law -> conditional wave continuum`.

This follow-up asks which parts can be promoted further.

The answer is sharply split:

- **Dimension:** the present branch really has only one continuous low-energy orbit direction.  Extra harmonic phases are internal massive shape variables.  The same remains true for the full scalar cyclic carrier.  Thus a second spatial-type coordinate requires new structure.
- **Geometry principle:** exact metric preservation is mathematically powerful but intrinsically one-dimensional as a sparse locality principle.  Generic higher-dimensional samples force the complete graph.  RNG is a cleaner dimension-agnostic candidate but its continuum bridge is open.
- **Refinement:** arbitrary-subdivision consistency genuinely forces `1/ell`; dyadic refinement alone does not.  The principle remains PM rather than strict-sourced.
- **Dynamics:** the static/refinement core does not select heat versus wave versus other dynamics, nor an absolute clock.  Bounded speed remains conditional.
- **Rank:** the strict spectrum fixes weights once rank is given, but does not source rank seven.

The main research frontier therefore moves away from further polishing of the current `S1` geometry.  The highest-value new object would be a genuinely higher-dimensional relational carrier with an independent source and a sparse proximity law that survives refinement.
